  "x-runtime-constraints": [
    "Input at most depth 16, 100000 visited nodes, strings 4096 bytes, array length 10000. Strict deny_unknown_fields throughout.",
    "update_values monthly_correction_percent count == months; rate > -100%; nonnegative money, fees and interest. Fees base = corrected principal + interest. Each correction and compound-interest period rounds to cents; simple interest rounds once.",
    "irrf_refund months unique; all money nonnegative; brackets start lower=0, contiguous [lower,upper), end upper=null or omitted, rates monotone in [0,100]. Deductions must not produce negative tax or downward boundary jump. Marginal model requires deduction=0; rate_minus_deduction computes full base * applicable rate - deduction. One user-supplied schedule for all rows; no implicit official tax source.",
    "undue_discounts factors >0, factor count=months per item, dates <= reference_date; total correction events <=12000. Double-refund manual hypothesis before correction. No statutory claim. No inferred date-to-period conversion.",
    "benefit_adjustment months strictly increasing, rates>-100%. No missing-month interpolation.",
    "currency_conversion numerator>=0 denominator>0; explicit unit names. Signed money allowed, round exact rational once; no historical currency or BRL assumption for converted units.",
    "Exponential and annuity formulas use f64 only after checked decimal/money decoding. Nonfinite/overflow/subflow returns Err. Final money max cents 9000000000000000; no fabricated zero/error swallowing.",
    "Computed rates use the declared rounding mode at eight decimal places; all financial_formula outputs include data.operation. simple_interest uses exact checked_i128_ratios; other formula operations disclose f64_experimental."
  ]
}
